@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using SpaceSails.Core
@*
    #251 · THE DOCKING FOCUS PANEL, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of NavHud.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that
    was in the HUD, character for character. Every member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME
    (fields keep their underscore, methods come across as delegates under their own names), which is what
    lets the markup move without a rewrite and lets MapMarkup splice it straight back where it came from.

    IHandleEvent repeats NavHud's own override, which repeats Map.Sim.cs's: the HUD's refresh belongs to
    OnTick's 200 ms throttle, and a child that did not repeat it would put an automatic render back on
    every event in here. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules; it exists to give the component
    Map.razor.css's scope (pinned in SpaceSails.Client.csproj), so every rule that styled these elements
    goes on matching them.

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block came out of a Razor CODE block, and
    a code block is where its first statements are legal. It is outside the fences, so what the source
    guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the HUD.
*@
@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from NavHud.razor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
            @* #200 · THE DOCKING FOCUS PANEL — "Own pop-up of the numbers to hit, just like in piracy-hold."
               The owner, inbound to Venus Haven, could not read off this HUD how close he was to the clamp's
               distance and speed limits; the line he had was one sentence of coaching, and the readout beside
               it toggled between whichever body was nearest. The flicker half is closed (#966's latch, #1033's
               Hill-sphere deferral). This is the other half, and it is deliberately the SAME BOX the piracy
               run already uses — the 🎯 autosteal criterion box on a prey dossier below: one row per gate,
               reading against required, green the moment the number is inside.

               ITS HOUSING IS THE PIRACY HOUSING. The plunder opportunity and the boarding progress are both
               in-FLOW sections of this same .map-readouts block, not floating cards, and so is this. That is
               the whole of its geometry answer (#1043): a box that claims real document height in a column
               already bound to the window (.map-flowcolumn, #992) cannot fight the nav-target lines above it
               or the Plotting panel below it for a pixel, and .map-readouts' own `overflow-y: auto` means it
               scrolls only when the window is genuinely too short. No z-index, no position, nothing to lose a
               stacking argument with.

               IT SPEAKS ON THE CLAMP'S OWN GATE. DockFocusLive is the affordance's phase — a dock haven
               armed or chosen, or the clamp in latched range of one — so a haven merely drifting past does
               not raise it, and being clamped on puts it away (the affordance is Hidden there). Every number
               in it comes off that same resolved affordance through DockFocus, whose gates are DockRule's
               constants: the panel and the ⚓ button are reading one judgement, so a row can never be green
               about a limit the arm refuses. #761: when the door refuses, the offending row is the one drawn
               outside its gate, and the verdict names it. *@
            @if (DockFocusLive)
            {
                <div class="map-dock-focus border border-secondary rounded px-2 py-1 mt-1">
                    <div class="fw-bold">⚓ Clamp at @(_dockAffordance.HavenName ?? "the berth") needs:</div>
                    @foreach (DockGateRow row in DockFocus.Rows(_dockAffordance, EffectiveDockTankPulses))
                    {
                        <div class="@(row.Inside ? "text-success" : "text-warning")">
                            @(row.Inside ? "✅" : "❌") @row.Label — @row.Reading @row.Gate
                        </div>
                    }
                    <div class="@(_dockAffordance.CanClampNow ? "text-success fw-bold" : "text-secondary")">
                        @DockFocus.Verdict(_dockAffordance, EffectiveDockTankPulses)
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}
